# HTL (HTML Template Language) Specification Reference

**Version:** 1.4  
**Authors:** Radu Cotescu, Marius Dănilă, Peeter Piegaze, Senol Tas, Gabriel Walt, Honwai Wong  
**License:** [Apache License 2.0](http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0.txt)  
**Status:** Final release  
**Release:** 18 June 2018  
**Source:** [Official HTL Specification](https://github.com/adobe/htl-spec/blob/master/SPECIFICATION.md)

## Overview

This document provides the complete HTL (HTML Template Language) specification as authoritative reference. All HTL implementations must conform to this specification.

## Rules for HTL Expression Language

### Expression Grammar Rules

**MANDATORY**: All HTL expressions MUST conform to the following grammar:

```ebnf
expression = '${' , [exprNode] , [ , '@' , optionList] , '}' ;
optionList = option {',' , option} ;
option = id [ , '=' , optionValues] ; 
optionValues = exprNode | '[' , valueList , ']' ;
valueList = exprNode {',' exprNode} ;
exprNode = orBinaryOp , '?' , orBinaryOp , ws , ':' , ws , orBinaryOp | orBinaryOp ;
orBinaryOp = andBinaryOp {, '||', andBinaryOp};
andBinaryOp = inBinaryOp {, '&&', inBinaryOp};
inBinaryOp = comparisonOp [, 'in', comparisonOp];
comparisonOp = factor [, comparisonOperator, factor];
comparisonOperator = '<' | '<=' | '==' | '>=' | '>' | '!=' ;
factor = term | '!' , term ;
term = propertyAccess | '(' , exprNode  , ')' | '[', valueList, ']' ;
propertyAccess = atom {'.' id} | atom {'[' , exprNode , ']'};
atom = string | id | int | float | bool ;
bool = 'true' | 'false' ;
id = ('a'..'z'|'A'..'Z'|'_') {'a'..'z'|'A'..'Z'|'0'..'9'|'_'|':'} ;
int = ['-']('1'..'9'){'0'..'9'} | '0' ;
float = ['-']('1'..'9'){'0'..'9'} '.' {'0'..'9'} [exponent] | ['-']'0.' ('0'..'9') {'0'..'9'} [exponent] | ['-']('1'..'9'){'0'..'9'} exponent ;
string = '"' {escSeq | -('\\' | '"')} '"' | '\'' {escSeq | -('\\'|'\'')} '\'' ;
```

**Grammar Conventions:**
- `foo` - Rule names
- `' '` - Terminals (literal characters)
- `|` - OR
- `[]` - Optional (zero or one)
- `{}` - Repetition (zero or more)
- `-` - "any character/sequence except"
- `..` - Range between terminals
- `,` - Optional whitespace

### Expression Syntax Rules

**REQUIRED**: Use the following expression syntax:

```html
<!-- Identifiers -->
${myVar}

<!-- Object member access -->
${myObject.key}
${myObject['key']}
${myObject[keyVar]}

<!-- Array index access -->
${myArray[1]}
${myArray[indexVar]}

<!-- Literals -->
${true}
${42}
${'string'}
${"string"}
${[1, 2, 3, true, 'string']}
```

**String Escaping Rules:**
- **REQUIRED**: Escape quotes: `\'` or `\"`
- **REQUIRED**: Escape backslash: `\\`
- **REQUIRED**: Escape expression start: `\${` to output literal `${`
- **Single character escapes**: `\t \b \n \r \f \' \" \\`
- **Unicode escapes**: `\u` followed by 4 hex digits (e.g., `\u0022` for `"`)

### Context-Sensitive Expression Rules

**MANDATORY**: HTL automatically applies context-aware XSS protection based on expression location.

```html
<tag>Some text ${myText}</tag>
<tag attr="Some text ${myAttrValue}"></tag>
<tag href="${myHrefValue}"></tag>
```

**Automatic URI Context Rules:**
- **REQUIRED**: The following attributes automatically use `uri` context:
  - `action` (`<form>`)
  - `cite` (`<blockquote>`, `<del>`, `<ins>`, `<q>`)
  - `data` (`<object>`)
  - `formaction` (`<button>`, `<input>`)
  - `href` (`<a>`, `<area>`, `<link>`, `<base>`)
  - `manifest` (`<html>`)
  - `poster` (`<video>`)
  - `src` (`<audio>`, `<embed>`, `<iframe>`, `<img>`, `<input>`, `<script>`, `<source>`, `<track>`, `<video>`)

**MANDATORY for Script/Style Contexts:**
- **REQUIRED**: Explicit context MUST be set for script and style contexts
- **REQUIRED**: If context is not set, expression outputs nothing

```html
<!-- Scripts -->
<a href="#whatever" onclick="${myFunctionName @ context='scriptToken'}()">Link</a>
<script>var ${myVarName @ context="scriptToken"}="Bar";</script>
<script>var bar='${someText @ context="scriptString"}';</script>

<!-- Styles -->
<a href="#whatever" style="color: ${colorName @ context='styleToken'};">Link</a>
<style>
    a.${className @ context="styleToken"} {
        font-family: '${fontFamily @ context="styleString"}', sans-serif;
        color: #${colorHashValue @ context="styleToken"};
        margin-${side @ context="styleToken"}: 1em;
    }
</style>
```

### Operator Rules

#### Logical Operators (Precedence Order)
**MANDATORY**: Operators evaluated in this order:

1. Grouping parenthesis: `()`
2. Logical NOT: `!`
3. Logical AND: `&&`
4. Logical OR: `||`
5. Conditional (ternary): `? :` (**REQUIRED**: `:` must have spaces around it)

```html
${varOne && !(varTwo || varThree)}  <!-- Precedence: 1 -->
${!myVar}                            <!-- Precedence: 2 -->
${varOne && varTwo}                  <!-- Precedence: 3 -->
${varOne || varTwo}                  <!-- Precedence: 4 -->
${varChoice ? varOne : varTwo}       <!-- Precedence: 5 - note spaces around ':' -->
```

**Rules:**
- `&&` and `||` return operand values (like JavaScript), not just boolean
- **REQUIRED**: Use `||` for default values: `${properties.pageTitle || properties.jcr:title || resource.name}`
- **REQUIRED**: Ternary operator `:` separator MUST be surrounded by spaces

#### Comparison Operators (Strict, No Type Conversion)
**REQUIRED**: All comparison operators are strict (like JavaScript `===` and `!==`)

```html
${nullValueOne == nullValueTwo}        <!-- Null comparison -->
${stringValueOne == stringValueTwo}    <!-- String comparison (strict) -->
${stringValueOne != stringValueTwo}    <!-- String comparison (strict) -->
${numberValueOne < numberValueTwo}     <!-- Number comparison -->
${numberValueOne <= numberValueTwo}    <!-- Number comparison -->
${numberValueOne == numberValueTwo}    <!-- Number comparison -->
${numberValueOne >= numberValueTwo}    <!-- Number comparison -->
${numberValueOne > numberValueTwo}     <!-- Number comparison -->
${booleanValueOne == booleanValueTwo}  <!-- Boolean comparison -->
${enumConstant == 'CONSTANT_NAME'}     <!-- Java Enum comparison -->
```

**Rules:**
- **REQUIRED**: `==` and `!=` are strict (no type conversion)
- **REQUIRED**: Operands MUST be same type for valid comparison

#### Relational Operator: `in`
**REQUIRED**: Use `in` operator for containment checks:

1. **String containment** (case-sensitive):
```html
${'a' in 'abc'}    <!-- returns true -->
${'ab' in 'abc'}   <!-- returns true -->
${'d' in 'abc'}    <!-- returns false -->
```

2. **Array/List containment**:
```html
${100 in myArray}  <!-- returns true if 100 in array -->
```

3. **Object/Map property/key check**:
```html
${'a' in logic}    <!-- returns true if object has property 'a' -->
```

### Type Casting Rules

#### Boolean Casting
**REQUIRED**: These values evaluate to `false`:
- `false`
- `0` (zero)
- `''` or `""` (empty string)
- `[]` (empty iterable)

**REQUIRED**: These values evaluate to `true`:
- `"false"` (non-empty string, even if content is "false")
- `[0]` (non-empty iterable)

#### String Casting
**REQUIRED**: Type conversion rules:

```html
${0}              <!-- outputs: 0 -->
${true}           <!-- outputs: true -->
${false}          <!-- outputs: false -->
${[1, 2, 3]}      <!-- outputs: 1,2,3 -->
${[true, false]}  <!-- outputs: true,false -->
${['foo', 'bar']} <!-- outputs: foo,bar -->
${['foo', '']}    <!-- outputs: foo, -->
```

### Expression Options Rules

**REQUIRED**: Options modify expressions using `@ optionName` or `@ optionName=value` syntax:

```html
<!-- Option without value -->
${myVar @ optName}

<!-- Option with identifier or literal -->
${myVar @ optName=myVar}
${myVar @ optName=true}
${myVar @ optName=42}
${myVar @ optName='string'}
${myVar @ optName="string"}
${myVar @ optName=[myVar, 'string']}

<!-- Multiple options -->
${myVar @ optOne, optTwo=myVar, optThree='string'}
```

### Parametric Expressions Rules

**REQUIRED**: Use parametric expressions (only options) for passing parameters to block elements:

```html
<tag data-sly-BLOCK="${@ paramOne, paramTwo=myVar, paramThree='string'}">element content</tag>
```

### Whitespace Rules

**REQUIRED**: Whitespace allowed between any part of expression:

```html
<!-- Recommended spacing style -->
${myVar @ argOne, argTwo=myVar, argThree='string'}

<!-- Spaces everywhere (also valid) -->
${ myVar @ argOne , argTwo = myVar , argThree = 'string' }
```

**Rules:**
- **RECOMMENDED**: No spaces around `@`, spaces after commas
- Whitespace is optional but recommended for readability

### Comments Rules

**HTL Comments:**
```html
<!--/* HTL comments are removed from output */-->
```
- **REQUIRED**: Syntax: `<!--/* */-->`
- **REQUIRED**: Cannot contain `*/-->` sequence
- **REQUIRED**: Completely removed from output

**HTML Comments with Expressions:**
```html
<!-- Page title: ${currentPage.jcr:title} -->
```
- **REQUIRED**: Expressions evaluated
- **REQUIRED**: Block statements ignored
- **REQUIRED**: Use for debugging output

## Display Context Rules

**MANDATORY**: All expressions MUST use appropriate display context for XSS protection.

| Context | When to use | What it does |
|---------|-------------|--------------|
| `attribute` | Default for attribute values | Encodes all HTML special characters |
| `attributeName` | Default for data-sly-attribute when setting attribute names | Validates attribute name, outputs nothing if validation fails |
| `elementName` | Default for data-sly-element | Validates element name, outputs nothing if validation fails |
| `html` | To safely output markup | Filters HTML to remove dangerous tags |
| `number` | To display numbers | Validates value is a number, outputs nothing if validation fails |
| `scriptComment` | Within JavaScript comments | Validates JavaScript comment, outputs nothing if validation fails |
| `scriptString` | Within JavaScript strings | Encodes characters that would break out of string |
| `scriptToken` | For JavaScript identifiers, literal numbers, or literal strings | Validates JavaScript token, outputs nothing if validation fails |
| `styleComment` | Within CSS comments | Validates CSS comment, outputs nothing if validation fails |
| `styleString` | Within CSS strings | Encodes characters that would break out of string |
| `styleToken` | For CSS identifiers, numbers, dimensions, strings, hex colours or functions | Validates CSS token, outputs nothing if validation fails |
| `text` | Default for content inside HTML Text Nodes | Encodes all HTML special characters |
| `unsafe` | When all other contexts are too restrictive | **Disables escaping and XSS protection completely** - USE WITH EXTREME CAUTION |
| `uri` | Default for `action`, `cite`, `data`, `formaction`, `href`, `manifest`, `poster`, `src` attributes | Validates URI, outputs nothing if validation fails |

**REQUIRED**: `elementName` context only allows these HTML5 semantic elements:

```
section, nav, article, aside, h1, h2, h3, h4, h5, h6, header, footer, address, main, 
p, pre, blockquote, ol, li, dl, dt, dd, figure, figcaption, div, a, em, strong, small, 
s, cite, q, dfn, abbr, data, time, code, var, samp, kbd, sub, sup, i, b, u, mark, ruby, 
rt, rp, bdi, bdo, span, br, wbr, ins, del, table, caption, colgroup, col, tbody, thead, 
tfoot, tr, td, th
```

**REQUIRED for HTML Comments**: Set explicit context:

```html
<!--[if IE]><link rel="shortcut icon" href="${site.root @ context='uri'}/images/favicon/favicon.ico?v2"><![endif]-->
```

## Format Option Rules

**REQUIRED**: Format option formats `Strings`, `Dates`, and `Numbers`.

**Format Type Detection:**
1. `type` option if present (`string`, `date`, `number`)
2. Placeholders (e.g., `{0}`) in pattern → string formatting
3. Type of `format` option object (`Date` or `Number`)
4. Default → string formatting

### String Formatting Rules

```html
${'Asset {0}' @ format=properties.assetName}
${'Asset {0}' @ format=[properties.assetName]}
${'Asset {0} out of {1}' @ format=[properties.current, properties.total]}
${'Asset {0} out of {1}' @ format=[properties.current, properties.total], i18n, locale='de'}
```

**REQUIRED**: Numbered parameters: `{0}`, `{1}`, etc.

### Date Formatting Rules

```html
${'yyyy-MM-dd' @ format=myDate}
${'yyyy-MM-dd' @ format=myDate, type='date'}
${'yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm' @ format=myDate, timezone='GMT+00:30'}
${'EEEE, dd MMMM yyyy' @ format=obj.date, locale='de'}
```

**REQUIRED Date Pattern Letters:**
- `y` (yy, yyyy) - Year
- `M` (MM, MMM, MMMM) - Month in year
- `w` (ww) - Week in year
- `D` (DD, DDD) - Day in year
- `d` (dd) - Day in month
- `E` (EEEE) - Day name in week
- `a` - Am/pm marker
- `H` (HH) - Hour in day (0-23)
- `h` (hh) - Hour in am/pm
- `m` (mm) - Minute in hour
- `s` (ss) - Second in minute
- `S` (SSS) - Millisecond
- `z` - General time zone
- `Z` - RFC 822 time zone
- `X` (XX, XXX) - ISO 8601 time zone

**REQUIRED**: Escape reserved letters with single quotes; escape single quotes as two in a row.

### Number Formatting Rules

```html
${'#.00' @ format=42}
${'#.00' @ format=myNumber, type='number'}
${'#,###.00' @ format=1000}
${'#.###;-#.###' @ format=obj.number}
${'#%' @ format=obj.number}
```

**REQUIRED Number Pattern Characters:**
- `0` - digit, shows as 0 if absent
- `#` - digit, does not show if absent
- `.` - decimal separator
- `-` - minus sign
- `,` - grouping separator
- `E` - separator between mantissa and exponent
- `;` - sub-pattern boundary (positive;negative)
- `%` - multiply by 100 and show as percentage

## i18n Option Rules

**REQUIRED**: Use `i18n` option for internationalization:

```html
${'Assets' @ i18n}  <!-- Translates to resource language -->
${'Assets' @ i18n, locale='en-US', hint='Translation Hint'}  <!-- Override locale with hint -->
```

**REQUIRED**: Special options when using `i18n`:
- `locale`: Overrides resource language (e.g., `en_US`, `fr_CH`)
- `hint`: Provides context for translators

## Array Join Option Rules

**REQUIRED**: Use `join` option to control array output:

```html
${['one', 'two'] @ join='; '}  <!-- outputs: one; two -->
<span class="${myListOfClassNames @ join=' '}"></span>
${'test' @ join=', '}  <!-- outputs: test (no change for strings) -->
```

## URI Manipulation Option Rules

**REQUIRED**: URI manipulation options:

### Scheme
```html
${'//example.com/path/page.html' @ scheme='http'}      <!-- outputs: http://example.com/path/page.html -->
${'http://example.com/path/page.html' @ scheme='https'} <!-- outputs: https://example.com/path/page.html -->
```

### Domain
```html
${'///path/page.html' @ domain='example.org'}  <!-- outputs: //example.org/path/page.html -->
${'http://www.example.com/path/page.html' @ domain='www.example.org'}  <!-- outputs: http://www.example.org/path/page.html -->
```

### Path Manipulation
```html
${'one' @ appendPath='two'}        <!-- outputs: one/two -->
${'path' @ prependPath='..'}       <!-- outputs: ../path -->
${'path/page.html' @ path='that/two'}  <!-- outputs: that/two.html -->
```

### Selectors
```html
${'path/page.woo.foo.html' @ selectors='foo.bar'}      <!-- outputs: path/page.foo.bar.html -->
${'path/page.woo.foo.html' @ addSelectors='foo.bar'}   <!-- outputs: path/page.woo.foo.foo.bar.html -->
${'path/page.woo.foo.html' @ removeSelectors='foo.bar'} <!-- outputs: path/page.woo.html -->
```

### Extension
```html
${'path/page' @ extension='html'}      <!-- outputs: path/page.html -->
${'path/page.json' @ extension='html'} <!-- outputs: path/page.html -->
```

### Suffix
```html
${'path/page.html' @ suffix='my/suffix'}  <!-- outputs: path/page.html/my/suffix -->
```

### Query
```html
${'http://www.example.org/search' @ query=jsuse.query, context='uri'}
${'http://www.example.org/search?s=1' @ addQuery=jsuse.query, context='uri'}
${'http://www.example.org/search?s=1&q=htl' @ removeQuery='q', context='uri'}
```

### Fragment
```html
${'path/page' @ fragment='fragment'}  <!-- outputs: path/page#fragment -->
```

## Block Statement Rules

### Block Statement Syntax Rules

**REQUIRED**: Block statements use `data-sly-*` attributes:

```html
<tag data-sly-BLOCK></tag>
<tag data-sly-BLOCK/>
<tag data-sly-BLOCK="string value"/>
<tag data-sly-BLOCK="${expression}"/>
<tag data-sly-BLOCK="${@ myArg='foo'}"/>
<tag data-sly-BLOCKONE="value" data-sly-BLOCKTWO="value"/>
```

**REQUIRED**: All evaluated `data-sly-*` attributes are removed from generated markup.

### Identifier Rules

**REQUIRED**: Block statements can use identifiers:

```html
<tag data-sly-BLOCK.IDENTIFIER="value"></tag>
```

**Rules:**
- **REQUIRED**: Top-level identifiers are case-insensitive (HTML attributes are case-insensitive)
- **REQUIRED**: Properties are case-sensitive

### data-sly-use Rules

**REQUIRED**: Use `data-sly-use` to expose logic:

```html
<div data-sly-use.page="customPage.js">${page.foo}</div>
<div data-sly-use.nav="${'Navigation' @ depth=1, showVisible=!wcmmode.edit}">${nav.foo}</div>
```

**Specification:**
- **Element**: always shown
- **Attribute value**: required; evaluates to `String`; object to instantiate
- **Attribute identifier**: optional; custom identifier name; if omitted, uses `useBean` identifier
- **Scope**: Global to script, available anywhere after declaration

**REQUIRED**: Element and content rendered (attribute removed from output).

**REQUIRED**: Parameters passed via expression options: `@ param1=value1, param2=value2`

### data-sly-text Rules

**REQUIRED**: Use `data-sly-text` to set element content:

```html
<p data-sly-text="${properties.jcr:title}">This text would never be shown.</p>
<p data-sly-text="${'<strong>Bold</strong>' @ context='html'}"></p>
```

**Specification:**
- **Element**: always shown
- **Content**: replaced with evaluated result
- **Attribute value**: required; evaluates to `String`
- **Auto XSS protection**: uses `text` context unless overridden
- **Falsy values**: Cast to strings (empty string/array output empty; `0` outputs "0", `false` outputs "false")

### data-sly-attribute Rules

**REQUIRED**: Use `data-sly-attribute` to set attributes:

```html
<tag class="className" data-sly-attribute.class="${myVar}"></tag>
<tag data-sly-attribute="${foobar}"></tag>  <!-- Multiple attributes from Map -->
```

**Specification:**
- **Element**: always shown
- **Content**: always shown
- **Attribute value**: optional; `String` for content, `Boolean` for boolean attributes, `Object` (Map) for multiple attributes
- **Attribute identifier**: optional; attribute name; must be omitted if value is `Object`
- **Processing order**: Left-to-right (later attributes override earlier)
- **Empty values**: Empty string removes attribute
- **XSS protection**: Attribute name and content automatically protected
- **RESTRICTIONS**: Cannot generate `on*` event handlers or `style` attribute (no safe context)

**REQUIRED**: Boolean values control boolean attributes:
```html
<input checked="${true}"/>    <!-- outputs: <input checked/> -->
<input checked="${false}"/>   <!-- outputs: <input/> -->
```

**REQUIRED**: Arrays cast to strings:
```html
<div title="${['one', 'two']}"></div>  <!-- outputs: <div title="one,two"></div> -->
<div title="${[]}"></div>               <!-- outputs: <div></div> (empty array removes attribute) -->
```

### data-sly-element Rules

**REQUIRED**: Use `data-sly-element` to replace element tag name:

```html
<div data-sly-element="${'h1'}">Blah</div>  <!-- outputs: <h1>Blah</h1> -->
```

**Specification:**
- **Element**: always shown
- **Content**: always shown
- **Attribute value**: required; `String`; element tag name
- **XSS protection**: `elementName` context (only allows specific HTML5 semantic elements)

### data-sly-test Rules

**REQUIRED**: Use `data-sly-test` for conditional rendering:

```html
<p data-sly-test="${wcmmode.edit}">You are in edit mode</p>
<p data-sly-test.editOrDesign="${wcmmode.edit || wcmmode.design}">displays when in edit or design mode</p>
<p data-sly-test>This paragraph will never display</p>
```

**Specification:**
- **Element**: shown if test evaluates to `true`
- **Content**: shown if test evaluates to `true`
- **Attribute value**: optional; evaluated as `Boolean` (not type-casted when exposed in variable); defaults to `false` if omitted
- **Attribute identifier**: optional; identifier name to access test result
- **Scope**: Global to script, available anywhere after declaration

**REQUIRED**: Identifier contains value as-is (not cast to Boolean).

### data-sly-list Rules

**REQUIRED**: Use `data-sly-list` to iterate:

```html
<ul data-sly-list="${currentPage.listChildren}">
    <li>${item.title}</li>
</ul>
<ul data-sly-list.childPage="${currentPage.listChildren}">
    <li>${childPage.title}</li>
</ul>
<ul data-sly-list="${currentPage.listChildren @ begin=0, end=9}">
    <li>${item.title}</li>
</ul>
```

**Specification:**
- **Element**: shown only if items > 0, or if value is string or number
- **Content**: repeated for each item
- **Attribute value**: optional; item to iterate over
- **Attribute identifier**: optional; iteration variable name; if omitted, uses `item`
- **Scope**: Available only in element's content scope; overrides outer scope but values restored after
- **Iteration options**: `begin`, `step`, `end` (all indices inclusive)

**REQUIRED**: Status object `itemList` (or `<variable>List`) available with:
- `index`: zero-based counter (0..length-1)
- `count`: one-based counter (1..length)
- `first`: `true` for first element
- `middle`: `true` if neither first nor last
- `last`: `true` for last element
- `odd`: `true` if count is odd
- `even`: `true` if count is even

**REQUIRED**: When iterating over `Map`, item variable contains key:

```html
<dl data-sly-list="${myMap}">
    <dt>key: ${item}</dt>
    <dd>value: ${myMap[item]}</dd>
</dl>
```

### data-sly-repeat Rules

**REQUIRED**: Use `data-sly-repeat` to repeat element (element shown once, content repeated):

```html
<p data-sly-repeat="${resource.listChildren}">${item.text}</p>
<p data-sly-repeat.childResource="${resource.listChildren}">${childResource.text}</p>
<div data-sly-repeat.article="${articlesCollection}" id="${article.id}">${article.excerpt}</div>
```

**Specification:**
- **Element**: shown only if items > 0, or if value is string or number
- **Content**: repeated for each item
- **Attribute value**: optional; item to iterate over
- **Attribute identifier**: optional; iteration variable name; if omitted, uses `item`
- **Scope**: Available only in element's scope
- **Iteration options**: `begin`, `step`, `end` (all indices inclusive)

**REQUIRED**: Same status object as `data-sly-list` available.

### data-sly-include Rules

**REQUIRED**: Use `data-sly-include` to include rendering script output:

```html
<div data-sly-include="template.html"></div>
<div data-sly-include="${'partials' @ appendPath='template.html'}"></div>
```

**Specification:**
- **Element**: always shown (but ignored, not displayed)
- **Content**: replaced with included script content
- **Attribute value**: required; file to include
- **Path options**: `appendPath`, `prependPath`
- **Scope**: Not passed to included template

**REQUIRED**: Comparable to JSP `<%@ include file="" %>`.

### data-sly-resource Rules

**REQUIRED**: Use `data-sly-resource` to include rendered resource:

```html
<section data-sly-resource="./path"></section>
<section data-sly-resource="${'./path' @ resourceType='my/resource/type'}"></section>
```

**Specification:**
- **Element**: always shown
- **Content**: replaced with resource content
- **Attribute value**: required; path to include (absolute or relative)
- **Options**: `appendPath`, `prependPath`, `selectors`, `addSelectors`, `removeSelectors`, `resourceType`
- **Scope**: Not passed to included resource

**REQUIRED**: Comparable to JSP `<jsp:include page="" />`.

### data-sly-template and data-sly-call Rules

**REQUIRED**: Use `data-sly-template` to declare templates:

```html
<template data-sly-template.one>blah</template>
<template data-sly-template.two="${@ title, resource='The resource of the parent node'}">
    <h1>${title}</h1>
    <p>Parent: ${resource.name}</p>
</template>
```

**Specification for `data-sly-template`:**
- **Element**: never shown
- **Content**: shown upon calling with `data-sly-call`
- **Attribute value**: optional; expression with only options, defining parameters
- **Attribute identifier**: required; template identifier to declare
- **Scope**: Global, available before or after definition

**REQUIRED**: Use `data-sly-call` to call templates:

```html
<div data-sly-call="${one}"></div>
<div data-sly-call="${two @ title=properties.jcr:title, resource=resource.parent}"></div>
<div data-sly-use.lib="templateLib.html" data-sly-call="${lib.one}"></div>
```

**Specification for `data-sly-call`:**
- **Element**: always shown
- **Content**: replaced with called template content
- **Attribute value**: required; expression defining template identifier and parameters
- **Scope**: Not inherited by template (must pass as parameters)

**REQUIRED**: Missing parameters initialize to empty string.

### data-sly-unwrap Rules

**REQUIRED**: Use `data-sly-unwrap` to hide element, show only content:

```html
<div data-sly-test="${myTest}" data-sly-unwrap>Foo</div>  <!-- Shows "Foo" if test is true -->
<div data-sly-unwrap="${myTest}">Foo</div>  <!-- Shows <div>Foo</div> if test is false -->
```

**Specification:**
- **Element**: shown if expression evaluates to `false`
- **Content**: always shown
- **Attribute value**: optional; evaluated as `Boolean`; defaults to `true` if omitted
- **Attribute identifier**: optional; identifier name to access result
- **Scope**: Global to script

### data-sly-set Rules

**REQUIRED**: Use `data-sly-set` to define identifiers:

```html
<span data-sly-set.profile="${user.profile}">Hello, ${profile.firstName}!</span>
<a href="${profile.url}">Edit profile</a>
```

**Specification:**
- **Element**: always shown
- **Content**: always shown
- **Attribute value**: optional; value to store
- **Attribute identifier**: required; identifier name to access stored value
- **Scope**: Global to script

## Block Statement Priority Rules

**MANDATORY**: When used on same element, block statements evaluated in this order:

1. `data-sly-template`
2. `data-sly-set`, `data-sly-test`, `data-sly-use`
3. `data-sly-call`
4. `data-sly-text`
5. `data-sly-element`, `data-sly-include`, `data-sly-resource`
6. `data-sly-unwrap`
7. `data-sly-list`, `data-sly-repeat`
8. `data-sly-attribute`

**REQUIRED**: When two block statements have same priority, evaluation is left-to-right.

## Special HTML Tags Rules

### `<sly>` Tag Rules

**REQUIRED**: Use `<sly>` tag to remove element, show only children:

```html
<sly data-sly-resource="./header"></sly>  <!-- Displays only header output, no <sly> tag -->
```

**REQUIRED**: Not a valid HTML5 tag but supported by HTL.

**REQUIRED**: To display `<sly>` tag in output:

```html
<sly data-sly-unwrap="${false}"></sly>  <!-- outputs: <sly></sly> -->
```

## Use-API Rules

**REQUIRED**: Business logic implemented through Use-API (separation of concerns).

### Java Use-API Rules

**REQUIRED**: Java Use-API objects:

1. **POJO with default constructor**:
```java
public class MyModel {
    private String title;
    // getters/setters
}
```

2. **POJO with `init` method**:
```java
public void init(javax.script.Bindings bindings);
```

**REQUIRED**: `bindings` map contains context objects for HTL script.

### JavaScript Use-API Rules

**DEPRECATED**: JavaScript Use-API deprecated for AEM Cloud Service. **REQUIRED**: Use Java Use-API instead.

**Legacy syntax** (for reference only):
```javascript
use(['dep1.js', 'dep2.js'], function (Dep1, Dep2) {
    return {
        propertyName: propertyValue,
        functionName: function () {}
    }
});
```

### Object Resolution Rules

**MANDATORY**: Property/method resolution follows this algorithm:

1. `expression.identifier` is equivalent to `expression["identifier"]` and `expression['identifier']`
2. Resolution algorithm:
   1. Try to resolve as publicly accessible field; if found, return
   2. Try to resolve as publicly accessible method without parameters:
      - Method named `identifier`; if found, call and return
      - Getter `getIdentifier` (camelCase); if found, call and return
      - Boolean getter `isIdentifier` (camelCase); if found, call and return
   3. Return `null` if not found

